You’re super close, but there are a few issues with the script you pasted:

. You cannot use `await` at the top level in a plain `<script>` block; it needs to be inside an async function.
. You must use template literals (\`\`) for multiline HTML in JS (not just plain HTML in the code).
. Always check that the DOM element exists before using it.

---

 Here’s a fixed, robust version you can drop in.

This includes the improved error handler, is wrapped in an async IIFE, and works anywhere in your HTML.

```html
<div id="recent-books-list"></div>
