 Add this CSS to your `<style>` block (anywhere inside your `<style>` tag):

```css
/ Make radio buttons larger /
input[type="radio"] {
 width: .em;
 height: .em;
 accent-color: fb; / Optional: match your indigo style /
 margin:  .em;
 vertical-align: middle;
}
```

If you want them even bigger, increase `.em` to something like `em`.

---

 Where to add this
Just append to your existing `<style>` in your template:

```html
<style>
 / ... existing styles ... /
 input[type="radio"] {
 width: .em;
 height: .em;
 accent-color: fb;
 margin:  .em;
 vertical-align: middle;
 }
</style>
```
You can also tune the `accent-color` to match your preferred palette!

