Absolutely! Here’s how you’d build a custom “Get Free Book” flow on your own website using BookFunnel’s Author API. This covers:

. Frontend: A form for the reader’s email (and maybe their name).
. Backend: Python Flask app that talks to BookFunnel’s API and returns a custom message or download link.
. Optional: Email delivery from your system, or redirect to the BookFunnel download page.

---

 ️⃣ Frontend Example (HTML/JS)

```html
<!-- index.html -->
<h>Get Your Free Book!</h>
<form id="get-book-form">
 <label>Email: <input type="email" name="email" required></label>
 <button type="submit">Claim Book</button>
</form>
<div id="response"></div>

<script>
document.getElementById('get-book-form').onsubmit = async function(e) {
 e.preventDefault();
 let email = this.email.value;
 document.getElementById('response').textContent = 'Processing...';
 let resp = await fetch('/api/get-book', {
 method: 'POST',
 headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
 body: JSON.stringify({ email })
 });
 let data = await resp.json();
 if (data.link) {
 document.getElementById('response').innerHTML = 
 `<a href="${data.link}" target="_blank">Download your book here!</a>`;
 } else {
 document.getElementById('response').textContent = data.message || 'Sorry, something went wrong.';
 }
};
</script>
```

---

 ️⃣ Backend Example (Python Flask)

Install dependencies: 
```bash
pip install flask requests
```

app.py:
```python
from flask import Flask, request, jsonify
import requests

BOOKFUNNEL_API_KEY = 'YOUR_BOOKFUNNEL_API_KEY'
BOOK_ID = 'YOUR_BOOKFUNNEL_BOOK_ID'  like 'BFxxxxxxxxxx'
BOOKFUNNEL_API_URL = 'https://api.bookfunnel.com/v/create_book_link'

app = Flask(__name__)

@app.route('/api/get-book', methods=['POST'])
def get_book():
 data = request.get_json()
 email = data.get('email', '').strip()
 if not email:
 return jsonify({'message': 'Email is required.'}), 

 resp = requests.post(
 BOOKFUNNEL_API_URL,
 headers={'X-BookFunnel-APIKey': BOOKFUNNEL_API_KEY},
 data={'object': BOOK_ID, 'email': email}
 )

 if resp.status_code == :
 res = resp.json()
 if res.get('link'):
 return jsonify({'link': res['link']})
 else:
 return jsonify({'message': res.get('message', 'No link returned.')})
 else:
 return jsonify({'message': 'Error connecting to BookFunnel.'}), 

if __name__ == '__main__':
 app.run(debug=True)
```

---

 ️⃣ How It Works

- User submits email on your branded form.
- Backend calls BookFunnel API with that email & your book’s ID.
- Receives a unique download link from BookFunnel.
- Frontend displays a direct download link, or a “Check your email!” message if you configure BookFunnel to email the user directly.

---

 ️⃣ Advanced Options

- Collect Name: Add a name field to your form and send it to BookFunnel if their API supports it.
- Double Opt-In: Email the BookFunnel link from your own server (using your email template/branding).
- Analytics: Log requests or trigger a webhook for your own CRM/newsletter list.

---

 ️⃣ Security/Spam Tips

- Throttle requests per IP/email to prevent abuse.
- Validate emails before sending to BookFunnel.

---

 ️⃣ Custom Success Message

Replace the download link with your own thank-you page, or use BookFunnel’s email delivery instead of showing the link (by using `/v/email_link`).

---

