GREAT follow-up! 
If your batch tags aren’t appearing in the URL when you click to page , that means your pagination links aren’t being updated by the JavaScript when the batch selection changes.

---

 How This Is Supposed to Work

. When you select batch tags, the JavaScript should update every pagination link (`<a class="pagination-link" ...>`) to append `&batch_tags=cover,scifi` (or whatever your tags are) to the URL.
. When you click “next” or any page, the new page’s URL includes your current tags, so your view/template can repopulate the Select.

---

 Why Isn’t It Happening?

Usually, one of these reasons:
- The JavaScript isn’t updating the links when you change batch tags.
- The links don’t have the `class="pagination-link"` that your JS selector looks for.
- The JS update runs before the pagination links are present in the DOM, or isn’t called at all.

---

 How to Fix/Ensure This

. Confirm your pagination `<a>` links have `class="pagination-link"`:
```django
<a class="pagination-link" href="?page=">next</a>
```
Do this for all pagination links.

---

. Your JS should update these links every time the batch tag selection changes:

```js
function updatePaginationLinks() {
 const currentBatchTags = $('batch-tag-select').val();
 let tagsQueryString = '';
 if (currentBatchTags && currentBatchTags.length > ) {
 tagsQueryString = '&batch_tags=' + currentBatchTags.map(encodeURIComponent).join(',');
 }
 $('.pagination-link').each(function() {
 let href = $(this).attr('href');
 if (href) {
 // Remove any existing batch_tags param before appending
 href = href.replace(/&batch_tags=[^&]/g, '');
 $(this).attr('href', href + tagsQueryString);
 }
 });
}
$('batch-tag-select').on('change', function() {
 updatePaginationLinks();
});
// Also run once on page load:
updatePaginationLinks();
```

---

. On page load and every batch select change, the links must have the new tags!

- After changing tags, inspect the "next" link: it should be like 
 `/tagger/?page=&batch_tags=cover,scifi`

---

 In Summary
- You must add `class="pagination-link"` to every pagination `<a>`.
- The JS must run `updatePaginationLinks()` both on page load and on tag selection change.

