When you change your batch tag selection (`batch-tag-select`), it makes sense to clear all checkboxes and reset the “Selected images” counter to zero (since you’re probably about to start a new tagging pass).

---

 How to Implement This

Add the following code to your JavaScript, inside the `DOMContentLoaded` handler (after Select is initialized):

```js
$('batch-tag-select').on('change', function() {
 // Clear all checkboxes
 $('.image-checkbox').prop('checked', false);
 // Update stored selection in sessionStorage
 saveSelectedImageIds([]);
 // Update the counter
 $('selected-count').text();

 // (Optional) Update pagination links as before
 updatePaginationLinks && updatePaginationLinks();
});
```

Make sure this runs after your `saveSelectedImageIds` and `updatePaginationLinks` functions are defined!

---

 What This Does
- When the batch tag selection changes:
 - All image checkboxes are unchecked
 - The sessionStorage “selectedImageIds” is cleared
 - The on-page selected count is reset to zero
 - Pagination links are updated as before

---

 Summary
- Copy-paste the above code in your JS, after Select and your sessionStorage helpers.
- Your “Selected images” counter will reset to zero whenever the batch tags change.

